WEBVTT

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:08.790
Wow.

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:10.830
[Mater] Mornin', Sally!

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:16.110
Hey, look at this here fancy new road
that Lightnin' McQueen done just made!

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:18.230
Yes! Uh, amazing!

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:22.310
Whoa-ho! Yeah! [sighing]

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:26.550
Oh, Ramone! Mama ain't
seen you that low in years.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.230
I haven't seen a road like this
in years.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:33.390
- Well, then let's cruise, baby.
- Low and slow.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.710
[Italian] È bellissima! It's beautiful!

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.510
Guido, look, it's-a like
it was paved by angels.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:41.750
Boy, I tell you what.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.630
I bet even the roads on the moon
ain't this smooth.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.390
Doc, look at this!

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:49.390
Shoulda tossed him into
the cactus a lot sooner, huh?

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:52.910
Well, he ain't finished yet.
Still got a long way to go.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:55.990
Guido, look at Luigi!

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:58.310
This is fantastico!

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:01.830
That looks like fun!
Mater, I got dibs, next turn!

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:06.230
Hey, Luigi, this new road
makes your place look like a dump.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:09.590
That crazy old devil woman.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:13.430
[sighs] Oh!

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.350
She's right!

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:16.990
- Ah!
- Guido!

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:20.830
Huh. That punk actually did a good job.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:25.910
Well, now... where the heck is he?

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:34.950
Sheriff!
Is he makin' another run for it?

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:38.430
No, no. He ran outta asphalt
in the middle of the night,

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.870
and asked me if he could
come down here.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:43.310
All he's tryin' to do
is make that there turn.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:46.230
[Lightning] No, no, no, no! Oh, great.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:49.230
Perfect turns on every track
I've ever raced on.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:55.390
Sheriff, why don't you go get yourself
a quart of oil at Flo's.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:56.870
I'll keep an eye on him.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:00.830
Well, thanks, Doc.
I've been feelin' a quart low.

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.350
[engine revving]

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:10.670
[screaming]

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.510
[spitting]

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.670
This ain't asphalt, son. This is dirt.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:20.510
Oh, great. What do you want?
You here to gloat?

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:23.910
You don't have three-wheel brakes,
so you got to pitch it hard,

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:27.470
break it loose and then
just drive it with the throttle.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:30.590
Give it too much, you'll be
outta the dirt and into the tulips.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:33.790
So you're a judge,
a doctor and a racing expert.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.510
I'll put it simple.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:39.750
If you're goin' hard enough left,
you'll find yourself turnin' right.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:46.190
Oh... Right. That makes perfect sense.
Turn right to go left! Yes! Thank you!

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.070
Or should I say, "No, thank you"?

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:51.750
Because in Opposite World,
maybe that really means, "Thank you"!

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:57.950
Crazy grandpa car. What an idiot!

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:01.070
[groans]

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:07.550
[Lightning] Turn right to go left.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.830
Hmm...

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:11.950
Whoa!

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:15.750
- Oh!
- [car crashing]

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:20.190
- Ow! Oh, that...
- [cactus crashing]

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:25.110
[screaming] Ow!

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:29.830
Turn right to go left.
Guess what. I tried it.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:32.990
You know what? This crazy thing
happened... I went right!

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:36.470
You keep talkin' to yourself,
people'll think you're crazy.

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:40.470
- Thanks for the tip.
- What? I wasn't talkin' to you!

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:50.950
- Oh, Guido, è bellissimo!
- Che cosa?

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:55.350
- It looks great! This is great!
- Ti piace, eh? Si, si, bellissimo.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:57.910
[grunts, passes gas]

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.950
Oh, Lord.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:01.670
- [chuckles]
- [Sheriff] Mater!

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.910
I need you
to watch the prisoner tonight.

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:07.270
Well, dad-gum! Wait a minute.
What if he tries to run again?

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.150
Just let him run outta gas
and tow him on back.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:12.710
- But keep an eye on him.
- Yes, sir!

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:15.470
[groaning] Oh...

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:18.230
While I'm stuck here
paving this stinkin' road,

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:20.830
Chick's in California schmoozing Dinoco.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:24.190
My Dinoco. Whoa, whoa, whoa!
Who's touching me?

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:26.550
You have a slow leak. Guido, he fix.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.630
You make-a such a nice new road.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.390
You come to my shop.
Luigi take-a good care of you.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.070
Even though you not a Ferrari.

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:37.230
You buy four tires,
I give you a full-a size spare

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:41.150
- absolutely free!
- Look, I get all my tires for free.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:44.790
[chuckling] I like your style, eh?

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:48.390
You drive the hard bargain.
OK. Luigi make you a new deal.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:51.950
You buy one tire,
I give you three for free!

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:53.670
[Flo] Oh, would you look at that?

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:55.870
Ramone, Ramone!

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:58.030
[Luigi] Then Luigi make you
a new new deal.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:01.110
[Lightning] No, no, no, no.
Deal me out. Pass. No, thank you.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:04.830
- No, no, no, no. No.
- This is it. My last offer.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:09.590
You buy one tire, I give you
seven-a snow tires for free!

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:12.510
Done. You interested, you call me.
You know where I am.

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:13.870
[exhales deeply]

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:15.110
Ah!

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:17.310
Stop! Let me...

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:21.510
Oh, Red, you missed a spot.
See it right there?

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:23.670
- No! No!
- On the hood right there.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:27.030
Stop, stop! That's cold!

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:29.630
Help! Please! Stop!

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:33.030
- [coughing, sputtering]
- Thanks, Red.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:35.550
What was that for?

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:37.750
- Do you want to stay at the Cozy Cone?
- Huh?

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:39.350
If you do, you gotta be clean.

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:41.910
'Cause even in hillbilly hell
we have standards.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:43.710
What, I...? I don't get it.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:46.390
I thought I'd say thank you
for doin' a great job.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:49.710
So I thought I'd let you stay with me.
I mean, not with me!

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:54.390
But there. Not with me there,
but there in your own cozy cone.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:58.350
- And I'd be in my cone, and it's...
- Wait. Wait, you're being nice to me.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:00.830
If you want to stay
at the dirty impound, fine.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:04.150
- I understand you criminal types.
- No, no, no, no. That's OK.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:07.390
- Yeah, the Cozy Cone.
- [Sally] It's newly refurbished.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:10.950
[Lightning chuckles] Yeah,
it's like a clever little twist.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:15.150
The motel's made out of caution cones,
which, of course, cars try to avoid.

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:18.590
But now we're gonna stay in them.
That's funny.

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:22.350
Figure that all out on your own,
did you?

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:25.750
Cone number one, if you want.

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:29.270
Oh...

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:34.110
Hey, do I spy a little
pinstriping tattoo back there?

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:37.270
Oh... [chuckles]
That's just a... Oh!

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:39.510
[both chuckle]

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:43.190
Oh, you saw that? Yeah.
Just gonna be going.

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:45.910
Gonna... Yeah.

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:53.230
- You know, I knew this girl Doreen.
- [gasps]

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:54.790
Good-lookin' girl.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:58.150
Looked just like a Jaguar,
only she was a truck!

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:01.750
You know, I used to crash into her,
just so I could spoke to her.

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:05.310
- What are you talking about?
- I don't know.

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:09.510
Hey, I know somethin' we can do tonight,
'cause I'm in charge of watchin' you!

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:13.750
No, Mater, I gotta finish this road,
and I have to get out of here.

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:17.390
Well, that's all right,
Mr. I Can't Turn On Dirt.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.750
You probably couldn't handle it anyway.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.590
Whoa, whoa, easy now, Mater.

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:24.630
You know who you're talkin' to?
This is Lightning McQueen.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:27.070
I can handle anything.

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:31.990
- [whispering] I'm not doin' this.
- Come on. You'll love it! [chuckles]

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:35.790
- [Mater] Tractor-tippin's fun.
- [Lightning] This is ridiculous.

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:38.310
- [tractors snore]
- [Mater] All right, listen.

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:42.350
When I say go, we go.
But don't let Frank catch you. Go!

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:44.270
Whoa! Wait! Who's Frank?

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:47.230
[Lightning whispering] Mater!

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:48.710
Wait, Mater!

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:51.830
OK, here's what you do.

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:55.350
You just sneak up in front of 'em,
and then honk.

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:57.910
And they do the rest. Watch this.

